    "title": "Founding Ferments: What Early America Brewed, Pressed, and Pickled",
    "excerpt": "The average colonist drank dozens of gallons of hard cider a year, and sobriety was never the point. Here is what a brand-new nation brewed, pressed, and pickled, and why surviving winter depended on it.",
